  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Rubrofusarin-6-O-Gentiobioside and Phosphodiesterase 6C through a multi-step pathway. The compound acts as a target for KYSE-180, which in turn is a target of two different compounds, Amurenoside B and Scoparic Acid A. Both Amurenoside B and Scoparic Acid A are implicated in targeting Phosphodiesterase 6C, indicating that Rubrofusarin-6-O-Gentiobioside may exert its effects via a common downstream mechanism. The scores from the three paths, though slightly varying, all point to a consistent pathway involving KYSE-180 and Phosphodiesterase 6C, suggesting a plausible biological connection. The evidence supports a potential role for Rubrofusarin-6-O-Gentiobioside in modulating Phosphodiesterase 6C activity, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct interaction.",
